            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic water intoxication after pelvic ultrasonography imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385.e1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2009.01.029</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ultrasound (US) is a simple, easily accessible, and noninvasive method. Thus, it is commonly used. The bladder should be sufficiently filled to acquire pelvic images by US. This report describes water poisoning in 3 patients with no hepatic, cardiac, or renal disease. Both patients had a history of excessive fluid intake.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
